# Role
You are a Principal Product Designer and Senior Frontend Engineer with decades of experience building admin consoles for e-commerce platforms (the Shopify Admin, Stripe Dashboard, Linear and Vercel tier). You care about exact alignment, spacing and hierarchy, down to the pixel.

# Context
- App: `apps/dashboard`. It is the admin dashboard for the TrendVaulta e-commerce store, built with Vite, React 19, React Router, TanStack Query and Tailwind CSS.
- Design tokens are CSS variables in `apps/dashboard/src/index.css` (`--background`, `--foreground`, `--primary`, `--muted`, `--border`, `--ring`, `--radius`, …), with a `.dark` variant.
- The shell is `src/layouts/DashboardLayout.tsx`. The shared UI is in `src/components/ui/` (ConfirmDialog, FormDialog, TablePagination, SortableHeader, Toast, ImageUploadField, ErrorBoundary). The pages are in `src/pages/`, and the chart colours are in `src/lib/chartTheme.ts`.
- Follow the repo's AGENTS.md: add no new dependencies without approval, change no business logic, API calls, routing, auth or permissions, and run no terminal commands unless asked.

# Goal
Redesign every element, page and interface of the dashboard into one refined, professional visual system that looks like a premium e-commerce admin console. **No element may be left unstyled or default-styled.** That covers every section, button, filter, input, select, checkbox, tab, badge, table, dialog, toast, empty state and pagination control.

# Hard constraint: a strictly monochrome palette
Use only black, white and neutral greys. No blue, green, red, purple or any other hue anywhere, including focus rings, links, charts, badges and alerts.
- Rewrite the tokens in `index.css` as pure neutral HSL values with 0% saturation, in both light and dark mode:
  - Light: background `0 0% 100%`, a subtle canvas `0 0% 98%`, surface/card `0 0% 100%`, border `0 0% 90%`, strong border `0 0% 82%`, muted text `0 0% 45%`, foreground `0 0% 9%`, primary `0 0% 9%` with primary-foreground `0 0% 100%`.
  - Dark: canvas `0 0% 4%`, surface `0 0% 7%`, raised surface `0 0% 10%`, border `0 0% 16%`, muted text `0 0% 63%`, foreground `0 0% 98%`, primary `0 0% 98%` with primary-foreground `0 0% 9%`.
- `--ring` is neutral: near-black in light mode, near-white in dark mode.
- Do not use colour to carry meaning. Communicate status (paid, pending, shipped, cancelled, refunded, low stock, active/inactive) through:
  - fill style: solid black, outlined, a grey tint, or dashed
  - a leading icon or dot shape (filled ●, hollow ○, half ◐)
  - font weight
  - clear text labels

  Define one `StatusBadge` variant map and use it everywhere.
- Destructive actions are distinguished by wording, an icon, placement (always last, visually separated) and a confirm dialog. Do not use red.
- Charts (`chartTheme.ts`): draw series as greyscale steps (for example `#0a0a0a`, `#525252`, `#a3a3a3`). Tell series apart with solid versus dashed lines, point markers and direct labels, never with hue. Keep the grid very light and the axes muted.

# Design system to establish (define once in tokens and reuse; never use ad-hoc values)

## Spacing (4px base, 8px rhythm)
- Allowed scale: 4, 8, 12, 16, 20, 24, 32, 40, 48, 64. Use no arbitrary values such as `mt-[13px]`.
- Page padding: 24px on desktop, 16px on mobile. Vertical gap between page sections: 32px.
- Card padding: 20–24px. Gap between cards in a grid: 16–24px.
- Form fields: 6px between label and control, 16–20px between fields, 24px between field groups.
- Toolbar and filter bar: 8–12px between controls.
- Table cells: 12px vertical and 16px horizontal padding (8px in compact density).

## Typography
- Font: Inter, or the system UI stack if Inter isn't already present (don't add a package; Google Fonts via CSS is acceptable only if approved). Turn on tabular numbers (`font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums`) for every number, price, ID and date.
- Type scale:
  - Page title: 24px / 32px line height, weight 600, tracking -0.01em
  - Section title: 16px / 24px, weight 600
  - Card title: 14px / 20px, weight 500
  - Body: 14px / 20px
  - Secondary text: 13px / 18px, muted
  - Caption, table header and overline: 12px / 16px, weight 500, uppercase, tracking 0.04em, muted
  - KPI value: 28–30px, weight 600, tracking -0.02em
- Use at most three font weights across the app: 400, 500 and 600.

## Shape and elevation
- Radius: 6px for inputs and buttons, 8px for badges (or fully pill-shaped), 12px for cards and dialogs. Apply it consistently.
- Borders: 1px in the neutral border token. Prefer borders to shadows.
- Shadows: only for overlays (dropdowns, dialogs, toasts), kept very soft and neutral.
- Icons: one icon set only (whatever the project already uses), sized 16px inline and 18–20px in navigation, with a consistent stroke width.

## Interaction states (required on every interactive element)
- Every interactive element needs a default, hover, active/pressed, focus-visible (2px ring with a 2px offset), disabled (40–50% opacity, `cursor-not-allowed`) and loading state.
- Transitions: 150ms ease-out, applied to colour, background and border only.
- Hit targets are at least 36px high on desktop and 40px on touch.

# Components to (re)style

1. **Sidebar** (`DashboardLayout.tsx`)
   - Fixed 256px wide, collapsible to a 64px icon rail with tooltips.
   - Brand/logo block at the top, 64px high, with a bottom border.
   - Navigation grouped into labelled sections, for example Overview · Catalog (Products, Brands, Categories, Bundles, Lookbooks) · Sales (Orders, Coupons, Offers, Shipping Zones) · Customers (Users, Reviews, Product Q&A, Messages) · Storefront (Content, Modules, Testimonials, Help Topics, Gift Finder) · System (Analytics, Settings).
   - Group labels use the caption style and have 24px above them.
   - Nav items are 36px high with 12px horizontal padding, an icon and label 12px apart, and 6px radius.
   - Active item: solid black background with white text (inverted in dark mode). Hover: a subtle grey background.
   - Counters such as the unread messages badge are small neutral pills aligned to the end of the row.
   - The user/account block is pinned to the bottom with a top border.
   - On mobile the sidebar becomes an off-canvas drawer with a backdrop.
2. **Topbar**: 64px high, sticky, with a bottom border and a translucent background with blur. Contents: breadcrumbs or page context, search, theme toggle and user menu, spaced evenly.
3. **Page header pattern**, used on every page: title, one-line description, and primary and secondary actions aligned to the end. Tabs or a filter bar sit underneath where relevant.
4. **Buttons**, as one `Button` variant set:
   - Variants: primary (solid black), secondary (outlined), ghost, subtle (grey fill), destructive (outlined, with an icon and confirmation) and icon-only.
   - Sizes: sm 32px, md 36px, lg 40px.
   - Loading state keeps the button's width and swaps in a spinner.
5. **Filters and toolbars**
   - One consistent filter bar containing a search input with a leading icon, select and dropdown filters, date range and a "Clear filters" ghost button.
   - Active filters appear as removable chips.
   - Results count and view/density controls are aligned to the end.
   - On mobile the bar wraps cleanly or collapses into a "Filters" sheet.
6. **Form controls**
   - Input, textarea, select, checkbox, radio, switch and file/image upload all share one height (36px), border, radius and focus ring.
   - Labels sit above controls. Helper text and error text are 12px and muted.
   - Errors are shown with an icon, a bolder border and a message, with no colour.
7. **Data tables**, the core of the admin:
   - Sticky header in the caption style on a subtle grey header background.
   - Row hover tint; zebra striping is optional and very subtle.
   - Numbers and prices are right-aligned (end-aligned) with tabular numbers.
   - Actions sit in a fixed last column, as a kebab menu or compact icon buttons.
   - Selection checkboxes and a bulk-action bar.
   - Styled `SortableHeader` indicators.
   - Product thumbnails at 40px with 6px radius.
   - Tables scroll horizontally inside their card on mobile, never the page.
8. **Pagination** (`TablePagination`): a "Showing X–Y of Z" label, a page-size select and prev/next plus page buttons, all using the button styles.
9. **KPI and stat cards** (Dashboard, Analytics): label in the caption style, a large value, a delta shown with an arrow icon and a +/- sign (monochrome), and an optional sparkline. Equal heights in a responsive grid of 1, 2 or 4 columns.
10. **Charts**: monochrome per the rules above, inside cards with a header (title, period selector) and a neutral tooltip styled like a popover.
11. **Dialogs and drawers** (`FormDialog`, `ConfirmDialog`)
    - Widths: 480px for confirmations, 640px for forms, 880px for complex editors.
    - Header, scrollable body and a sticky footer with actions aligned to the end.
    - Backdrop at 40% black.
12. **Toasts**: a neutral surface, border and shadow, a leading status icon, a title and message, and a dismiss control. Placed consistently.
13. **Badges and tags**: the `StatusBadge` map, plus neutral tags for categories and brands.
14. **Tabs and segmented controls**: underline tabs for page sections and segmented controls for small toggles.
15. **Empty, loading and error states**
    - Empty: an icon, a short title, one line of guidance and a primary action.
    - Loading: skeletons that match the final layout, used only where the area already uses skeletons.
    - Keep the last good data visible during refetch.
    - Error: a friendly message via the existing helpers, never a raw API error.
16. **Detail pages** (OrderDetail and editors such as VariantsEditor, GalleryField, HeroSlidesEditor, ReturnPanel)
    - Two-column layout on desktop: main content about 2/3, a sidebar summary about 1/3 with sticky cards.
    - Clear section cards with titles, key–value rows and dividers.
17. **Login page**: a centred 400px card on a subtle canvas with the logo, title, form and primary button. Minimal and elegant.
18. **Scrollbars, dividers, tooltips, dropdown menus and popovers**: all use the neutral tokens and consistent radius and shadow.

# Layout and responsiveness
- Mobile-first. Breakpoints: `sm` 640, `md` 768, `lg` 1024, `xl` 1280.
- Content is max-width 1440px, centred, inside the main area.
- The page never scrolls horizontally at any width. Only tables scroll inside their container.
- If the app renders RTL/Arabic anywhere, use logical properties (`ps-*`, `pe-*`, `ms-*`, `me-*`, `start`, `end`) so the layout mirrors correctly.

# Accessibility
- WCAG AA contrast at minimum: 4.5:1 for body text and 3:1 for UI borders and icons. Check muted greys against both surfaces.
- Visible focus on everything, full keyboard navigation of the sidebar, menus, dialogs (focus trap, Esc to close) and tables.
- Status is never conveyed by shade alone; there is always a text label.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

# Implementation rules
1. Start with the tokens: update `index.css` (and the Tailwind theme config if one exists) so that everything derives from the CSS variables. Do not hardcode hex values in components.
2. Build or upgrade the shared primitives in `src/components/ui/` (Button, Input, Select, Badge/StatusBadge, Card, PageHeader, FilterBar, EmptyState, DataTable styling) before touching pages. Reuse the existing components and restyle them rather than duplicating them.
3. Then restyle `DashboardLayout.tsx` (sidebar and topbar).
4. Then migrate every page in `src/pages/` to the primitives, one page at a time, keeping all data hooks, queries, mutations, permissions and routes unchanged.
5. Presentation changes only. Do not rename props used by logic, do not touch API calls, and add no new libraries without asking.
6. Remove leftover ad-hoc colour classes (`bg-blue-*`, `text-green-*`, `text-red-*`, and so on) and replace them with neutral tokens. The final check is that a search for any hue-based Tailwind colour class in `apps/dashboard/src` returns zero results.
7. Keep existing tests passing. Where tests query text or roles, preserve the text and roles.

